   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The numerator has the form \\( f(\\frac{\\pi}{2} + h) - f(\\frac{\\pi}{2}) \\) with \\( f(x) = \\sin x \\), because \\( f(\\frac{\\pi}{2}) = 1 \\).",
         "mathjson": 1
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "So the function is \\( f(x) = \\sin x \\) and the base point is \\( x = \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            "Pi",
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The limit is the definition of \\( f'(\\frac{\\pi}{2}) \\), and \\( f'(x) = \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Cos",
            "x"
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "Evaluate: \\( f'(\\frac{\\pi}{2}) = 0 \\).",
         "mathjson": 0
      }
